+# Little Library
+
+A small, single-user reading tracker. Books are stored in `data/books.json` and served with a lightweight Node.js server—no database or account required.
+
+## Run it
+
+Requires Node.js 18 or newer.
+
+```sh
+npm start
+```
+
+Then open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000). Use `npm run dev` to restart the server automatically during development. Set `PORT` to use a different port.
+
+## Reading shelf
+
+- Add a title, author, and optional notes from the shelf.
+- Switch between currently reading and finished books, and mark books finished.
+- Open a book’s individual `/books/<id>` page to read its notes or copy its shareable link.
+- Remove a book from its shelf card or detail page.
+
+Back up `data/books.json` to keep a copy of your shelf. A shared link opens the same book on the same app; there are no accounts or remote hosting built in.
